WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.905 --> 00:00:15.688
Once upon a time, there lived a farmer who had a vineyard.

2
00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:20.270
Though the vineyard was small, the farmer worked hard and took good care of it.

3
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.193
In this way, he provided his three sons with a good, happy life.

4
00:00:25.913 --> 00:00:28.214
The farmer loved his sons very much.

5
00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:34.290
They had plenty of food, which pleased the oldest son, who loved to eat.

6
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.832
They had comfortable beds, which pleased the middle son, who loved to sleep.

7
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:45.336
They had fine clothing, which pleased the youngest son, who loved wearing fancy clothes.

8
00:00:46.176 --> 00:00:48.598
The sons had everything they needed and wanted.

9
00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:51.479
This made the farmer proud.

10
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.001
Many years passed.

11
00:00:55.782 --> 00:00:59.444
The farmer grew old, but he still went out to the vineyard every day.

12
00:01:00.452 --> 00:01:02.893
One day he fell from a ladder while working.

13
00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:06.194
He decided to speak to his children.

14
00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:12.615
sons," the farmer said.

15
00:01:12.636 --> 00:01:16.697
"I am too old and weak to continue working.

16
00:01:17.537 --> 00:01:21.578
Someone must tend the vineyard, or we will have no money.

17
00:01:22.418 --> 00:01:25.939
It's time for you three to start working."

18
00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.280
The oldest son rolled his eyes.

19
00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.870
"I'm too hungry to work."

20
00:01:31.911 --> 00:01:33.051
The middle son yawned.

21
00:01:33.071 --> 00:01:35.854
"I'd rather take a nap."

22
00:01:37.795 --> 00:01:38.976
The youngest frowned.

23
00:01:38.996 --> 00:01:41.498
"I don't want to get my clothes dirty."

24
00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:44.601
The farmer shook his head in disgust.

25
00:01:44.621 --> 00:01:49.605
"How did I raise such lazy, selfish sons?"

26
00:01:50.165 --> 00:01:50.666
he thought.

27
00:01:51.947 --> 00:01:54.709
Over time, the farmer found himself growing weaker.

28
00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.412
Soon the house fell into disrepair.

29
00:01:59.316 --> 00:02:03.259
The vineyard became neglected and overgrown with weeds and tangled vines.

30
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.564
The farmer knew he had little time left, and he despaired over his lazy sons.

31
00:02:10.525 --> 00:02:13.047
One night the farmer called them to his bedside.

32
00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:17.330
"My sons, I will not live much longer.

33
00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:22.074
There is something I must tell you before I die.

34
00:02:22.995 --> 00:02:27.318
There is a very special treasure in the vineyard.

35
00:02:28.359 --> 00:02:31.229
Find it, and it is yours."

36
00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:34.209
The old man passed away that night.

37
00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.971
The sons forgot about the treasure for a while.

38
00:02:39.731 --> 00:02:43.812
But then the oldest noticed they were running out of food—and money.

39
00:02:43.832 --> 00:02:49.834
"Maybe Father's treasure is money," he said.

40
00:02:49.854 --> 00:02:52.555
"Yes," the middle son said.

41
00:02:52.575 --> 00:02:56.156
"Father's vineyard was successful before he stopped working."

42
00:02:57.312 --> 00:02:59.953
"If we find that treasure, we'll never have to work!"

43
00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.253
the youngest said.

44
00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.434
The sons went out right away.

45
00:03:03.454 --> 00:03:07.435
"The vineyard is overgrown!"

46
00:03:07.915 --> 00:03:09.055
the youngest son said.

47
00:03:10.136 --> 00:03:11.236
The middle son nodded.

48
00:03:11.256 --> 00:03:13.637
"We'll never find the treasure here."

49
00:03:13.657 --> 00:03:18.918
"We have to tend the vineyard first," the oldest said.

50
00:03:20.378 --> 00:03:22.359
They cleared the weeds and trimmed the vines.

51
00:03:23.279 --> 00:03:25.860
The soil was too hard to dig, so they watered it.

52
00:03:27.648 --> 00:03:29.409
But they saw no sign of the treasure.

53
00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.231
Every day the sons checked the vineyard, but they didn't find the treasure.

54
00:03:37.251 --> 00:03:42.032
"Look!" the youngest cried one day.

55
00:03:42.692 --> 00:03:43.892
His brothers ran to him.

56
00:03:43.912 --> 00:03:47.873
"Did you find the treasure?"

57
00:03:48.354 --> 00:03:48.954
one asked.

58
00:03:48.974 --> 00:03:51.054
"No," the youngest said.

59
00:03:51.074 --> 00:03:53.195
"But grapes are growing again.

60
00:03:54.055 --> 00:03:54.775
Should we pick them?"

61
00:03:55.556 --> 00:03:56.976
The middle son looked at the grapes.

62
00:03:57.976 --> 00:03:59.177
"Maybe we should pick them.

63
00:03:59.878 --> 00:04:01.019
We could sell them for money."

64
00:04:01.039 --> 00:04:03.961
"Good idea," the oldest said.

65
00:04:03.981 --> 00:04:06.884
"We can look for the treasure later."

66
00:04:08.745 --> 00:04:09.886
Several years passed.

67
00:04:11.187 --> 00:04:15.151
The sons never saw any sign of the treasure, but the vineyard kept them busy.

68
00:04:15.991 --> 00:04:17.893
They watered the soil and pulled the weeds.

69
00:04:18.714 --> 00:04:20.555
They picked grapes and tended the vines.

70
00:04:21.196 --> 00:04:25.780
Eventually they stopped looking for the treasure, never realizing they had already found it.

71
00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.350
The vineyard was successful again, thanks to the sons' hard work.

72
00:04:31.693 --> 00:04:34.059
That was the true treasure in the vineyard.
